# ====== Java / Spring Boot ======
*/target/
*.jar
*.war
*.class
*.log

# ====== Node / React ======
*/node_modules/
*/build/
*/dist/
*/coverage/
# .env at repo root — this is the actual secrets file (JWT_SECRET, DB/RabbitMQ
# passwords) created via `cp .env.example .env`. The original pattern here was
# `_env` (a typo — matches a literal filename "_env", not dotfiles) plus
# `*/.env`, which only matches .env inside a subdirectory. Neither pattern
# covers the root .env, so it was never actually gitignored — a real risk of
# committing live secrets. Both now fixed below.
.env
.env.local
*/.env
*/.env.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ====== Misc ======
*.zip
.github/
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example

# ====== IDE / Editors ======
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.project
